# Safrico — Cursor Rules

## Project

Safrico is a crop inventory management app built on the AI-optimized Next.js starter. Domain features live in `src/features/`.

## Before Writing Code

1. Read `docs/requirements.md` or `docs/PRD.md` for the current feature
2. Follow the vertical slice pattern in `src/features/projects/`
3. After changes run: `bun run lint && npx tsc --noEmit && bun test`

## Feature Slice Structure

Every new feature in `src/features/{name}/`:

- `models.ts` — re-export Drizzle table + inferred types
- `schemas.ts` — Zod v4 validation (`import { z } from "zod/v4"`)
- `errors.ts` — error classes with `code` and `statusCode`
- `repository.ts` — database queries only
- `service.ts` — business logic, access control, logging
- `index.ts` — public API (export service, not repository)
- `tests/` — schemas, errors, service tests

## Database

- Add tables in `src/core/database/schema.ts`
- Run `bun run db:push` after schema changes

## API Routes

- Place routes in `src/app/api/{feature}/`
- Auth via Supabase `createClient()` from `@/core/supabase/server`
- Use `handleApiError` from `@/core/api/errors`

## Logging

Use `getLogger("feature.component")` with `_started`, `_completed`, `_failed` suffixes.

## Do Not

- Import repository from outside the feature slice
- Use `console.log` — use structured logger
- Use default exports except Next.js pages/layouts
- Skip tests for new service logic
